<h1>Emmett Plant Exits as Xiph.Org <abbr title='Chief Executive Officer'>CEO</abbr></h1>
<p>
The Xiph.Org Foundation today announced the termination of its contracting
relationship with Emmett Plant.  He served as acting CEO since May 2002,
working to build relationships with certain strategic partners in order
to further the Foundation's efforts.</p>

<p>
The Foundation is a publicly supported non-profit corporation that was
recently granted a favorable advance ruling on 501(c)(3) exemption by the
<abbr title='Internal Revenue Service'>IRS</abbr>.
In accordance with this ruling, the Foundation will enter a new phase of
planning and operation.  Xiph.Org will be focusing its financial efforts
in order to develop public funding sources and will be announcing several
initiatives toward that end in the next few months.</p>

<p>
The Foundation provides a home for a collection of open source
multimedia-related projects.  The Foundation’s purpose is to support and
develop free, open protocols and superior software to serve the public,
developers and business markets.
</p>

